# Meowdoku environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Everything here is optional: with no .env file
# at all the app builds, installs and plays exactly as it always has. Only
# multiplayer reads any of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_PARTY_HOST — where the party server lives. Host and optional port, no
# scheme and no trailing slash:
#
#     127.0.0.1:8787
#     meowdoku-party.pre0.workers.dev
#
# Loopback hosts are addressed over http/ws, everything else over https/wss.
#
# Unset is a meaningful value. A build with no party host is a single-player
# build: the home screen hides multiplayer rather than offering a button that
# can only fail, and none of the multiplayer chunk is ever requested. That is
# also what a fork of this repo gets by default, which is the point.
#
# Local development:
#
#     pnpm party:dev     # wrangler, serving the room server on :8787
#     pnpm dev           # vite, in a second terminal
#
# `pnpm dev` is a Vite server and sends no Content-Security-Policy, so a local
# party host on any port works without further configuration. `vercel dev` does
# apply vercel.json, and will block a loopback party host — use `pnpm dev`.

VITE_PARTY_HOST=127.0.0.1:8787

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On Vercel
#
# Set VITE_PARTY_HOST for Production and Preview (Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables) to the deployed Worker's hostname. It is read at build
# time, not at runtime, so changing it needs a redeploy.
#
# The same hostname must also appear in the Content-Security-Policy in
# vercel.json, in `connect-src`, as BOTH an https:// and a wss:// origin — the
# browser refuses the health probe and the WebSocket otherwise, and a CSP is not
# something an environment variable can widen. Two places, deliberately: the
# policy is a security boundary and is reviewed as source, not configured per
# environment. tests/unit/offline-guard.test.ts checks the shape of what is
# there, and README.md records which host it names.
